  "description": "The NUMERIC half of the browse-key filter at :206-219, which is the limb no other case in this folder reaches. TRNIDINI is not spaces, so :206 is false and control takes the ELSE at :208; the sixteen characters typed are all digits, so IS NUMERIC at :209 is true and :210 MOVE TRNIDINI OF COTRN0AI TO TRAN-ID copies them into the RIDFLD width for width. WS-ERR-FLG is NOT set, so nothing downstream short-circuits and the reject limb at :211-217 is not entered. Note what IS NUMERIC costs the operator on a PIC X(16) item: every one of the sixteen positions is examined, so a short entry that arrives space padded is not numeric and is refused - the key declared here is a full-width sixteen-digit identifier for exactly that reason. POSITIONING, derived rather than assumed: :597 has GTEQ commented out, and GTEQ is the STARTBR default, so commenting it out changed nothing and the browse positions at-or-after the RIDFLD, inclusive of the anchor record. The other cases in this folder corroborate it - they browse from LOW-VALUES and are served the first record on file, which only an inclusive at-or-after positioning produces. And because the key pressed is ENTER, the combined relation at :285 (NOT = DFHENTER AND DFHPF7 AND DFHPF3) is false, so no skip read discards the anchor: record 08 - the record AT the typed key - is screen row one, and rows one to ten take records 08 to 17. The look-ahead READNEXT at :308 then finds record 18, so :310 SET NEXT-PAGE-YES. Exactly ONE send, from :326, because this is the REENTER path at :118-121 and no read reported end-of-data. The page number is reset before it is incremented: the commarea arrives at page two and :224 MOVE 0 TO CDEMO-CT00-PAGE-NUM overwrites it, so :306-307 computes 0 + 1 = 1 rather than 2 + 1 = 3 - which is what makes the reset observable rather than inferred. The typed key is then cleared from the redisplayed screen twice over, by :325 inside PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD and again by :228 once it returns, so TRNIDINO comes back as spaces. The ten-way selection scan at :148-182 takes its WHEN OTHER at :179-181 because all ten SEL000nI cells are spaces, which leaves CDEMO-CT00-TRN-SEL-FLG and CDEMO-CT00-TRN-SELECTED spaces and makes :183 false, so no transfer is attempted. This case is also the folder's carrier for the four display-format edges of POPULATE-TRAN-DATA at :381-445, all four seeded INSIDE the ten-row window. TRAN-AMT is S9(09)V99 and WS-TRAN-AMT is PIC +99999999.99 at :56, so :383 renders twelve characters - one sign position that is always occupied, eight integer positions, a point and two decimals. Record 09 holds -1234.56 and renders -00001234.56, the only negative sign in the folder. Record 11 holds 0.00 and renders +00000000.00, because PIC + emits a plus for zero rather than a space. Record 13 holds 987654321.99, which has NINE integer digits where the mask has eight: a numeric MOVE truncates on the LEFT, so the leading 9 is discarded and the row renders +87654321.99. That is legacy behaviour to reproduce, not a mask to widen. Record 15 carries a fifty-character TRAN-DESC where TDESC08I is PIC X(26), and an alphanumeric MOVE truncates on the RIGHT, so the row paints 'PURCHASE OF PROFESSIONAL S' - twenty-six characters ending mid-word. Both truncations happen in the one paragraph and at opposite ends. Records 13 and 15 also carry origination timestamps in different years from every other row, so TDATE renders 11/07/23 and 12/31/21 against a pinned clock reading 07/19/22: the row date comes from TRAN-ORIG-TS through :384-388 and never from FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE at :569. The class is TransactionMenuController because the build prompt names it so; the program LISTS transactions ten to a page, and there is no menu anywhere in its 699 lines. PROVENANCE: every value here was derived statically, by reading app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl against the byte offsets of app/cpy/CVTRA05Y.cpy, the field widths of app/cpy-bms/COTRN00.CPY and app/bms/COTRN00.bms, and the file definition in app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD. It was never captured from a live COBOL run: no z/OS, no CICS emulator and no indexed-file COBOL runtime is available here, and DFHAID, DFHBMSCA and DFHATTR are absent from the repository.",
